      "issue_description": "A vulnerability exists in decompress_smooth_data() where, for malformed progressive JPEG images containing an interleaved Y/Cb/Cr DC scan followed by two non-interleaved Y DC scans, the prev_coef_bits[] array is initialized only for the Y component and not for Cb and Cr. The uninitialized values for Cb and Cr are transferred to the prev_coef_bits_latch[] array in smoothing_ok(), and when cinfo->master->last_good_iMCU_row is 0, decompress_smooth_data() reads these uninitialized values while attempting to smooth the second iMCU row.\n"
    },
